            <div xml:id="d743">

                <pb facs="0953" n="943" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg943"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.93/1–747: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-01-15T16:00:00-05:00">January 15, 1947—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>60. Matter discussed informally with Navy which states necessary processing in
                    field applications by Marine personnel will consume considerable amount time and
                    therefore no departure dependents contemplated immediate future. (Embtel 36, Jan
                    7) Problem will be presented General Marshall his arrival Washington.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
